      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DEBATING (3) has improved in each run back from a spell, and he will be peaking third up from a spell. A 2kg claim will mean he carries the same weight as his last start, and he can take this out. DUMMY SPIT (2) is normally very consistent at this level, and even though he was a touch plain last start, he will have Jarrod Todd back in the saddle for this. With the right run, he can break his win drought in this. BRYCE (4) has raced his way back into some good form, and dropping back from 1600m to 1200m, while not ideal, should not bother him too much. Each way claims again. I'M A DREAMER (1) went back-to-back to open this season at Kununurra, and he races just as well around this circuit. He will need luck from a tricky gate over this shorter trip, but he can complete the hat-trick. SASS (6) made the most of her best draw in a while when leading all the way to score here nearly 4 weeks ago by half a length. She lands the pole position again and can repeat the dose.",
